  "equipment_type": "Commercial Wi-Fi thermostat",
  "applies_to": "Carrier Connect Wi-Fi thermostats 33TCSPF-4 (Carrier branded) and 33TWSPF-4 (unbranded), 24 VAC touchscreen thermostats with built-in BACnet.",
  "summary": "The Connect 33TCSPF-4 / 33TWSPF-4 thermostat exposes 149 BACnet objects (plus two network port objects) over BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP over Wi-Fi (it has an MS/TP network port object and an IPv4 network port object). Compared with the earlier 33CONNECTSTAT43 list it adds outdoor air quality values, standby setpoints, hydronic fan coil and analog output (hot water valve) points, door switch points and network general purpose outputs. Configuration objects are gated: they only accept writes after BACnet Config Write Enable is turned on.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Carrier's tables call value objects 'Analog Variable' / 'Binary Variable'; they are AV and BV objects.",
    "Access mapping: READ_ONLY = R; READ_WRITE and GATED_WRITE = W (GATED_WRITE needs BV 511 CFG_WR_EN enabled); WRITE_WHEN_OOS (the three AIs) = R, writable only when the object is out of service.",
    "BV 916 LOCKOUT_FAIL is printed as removed (changed from a fault to a system event) and is left out.",
    "The 33TWSPF-4 has its own guide (11-808-1227-01) with the same object appendix.",
    "Multistate state numbers (1, 2, 3...) follow the printed order of the state list; MV 509 states continue across a page break."
  ],
